  "title": "A link invariant from quantum dilogarithm",
  "authors_raw": "ENSLyon, 46 All\u00e9e d\u2019Italie",
  "abstract": "The link invariant, arising from the cyclic quantum dilogarithm via the particular R-matrix construction, is proved to coincide with the invariant of triangulated links in S3 introduced in [14]. The obtained invariant, like Alexander-Conway polynomial, vanishes on disjoint union of links. The R-matrix can be considered as the cyclic analog of the universal R-matrix associated with Uq(sl(2)) algebra. ENSLAPP-L-517/95 \u2217On leave from St. Petersburg Branch of the Steklov Mathemati cal Institute, Fontanka 27, St. Petersburg 191011, RUSSIA \u2020URA 14-36 du CNRS, associ\u00b4 ee ` a l\u2019E.N.S. de Lyon, et ` a l\u2019Universit` e de Savoie 0",
